  "prefLabel": "Eng 106.01 Committees",
  "priorExpiration": "1998-09-17",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Eng 106.01 Committees.\n\n(a) A committee shall consist of one or more of board members who have been directed by the board to investigate and make recommendations on matters which could be handled by the full board.\n\n(b) When expressly authorized by the board, the authority of a committee shall include:\n\n(1) The retention of voluntary assistance from qualified non-board members; and\n\n(2) The retention of paid advisors or consultants pursuant to RSA 332:G-3.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Eng 100) #5397, eff 5-20-92; ss by #6752, Interim, eff 5-20-98, EXPIRED: 9-17-98\n\nNew. #6910, eff 12-15-98\n\nAPPENDIX\n\nRule | Statute\n\nEng 101 | RSA 310-A:3\n\nEng 102 | RSA 541-A:54\n\nEng 103 | RSA 310-A:3\n\nEng 104.01 | RSA 541-A:16, I(a); RSA 91-A:4\n\nEng 104.02 | RSA 541-A:16, I(a); RSA 91-A:4\n\nEng 105 | RSA 310-A:3, RSA 541-A:16 I, (a)\n\nEng 106 | RSA 310-A:3, RSA 541-A:16 I, (a)",
